1 NAME Angus Og /MacDonald/ 8th of Dunnyveg
2 GIVN Angus Og
2 SURN MacDonald
2 NSFX 8th of Dunnyveg
2 _MARNM MacDonnell
1 NAME Angus MacDonnell, of Dunnyveg and the Glens
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1539
2 PLAC Dunnyveg
2 ADDR
3 CTRY Scotland
1 BURI
2 DATE 1614
2 ADDR
3 STAE Argyll
3 CTRY Scotland
1 DEAT
2 DATE 21 OCT 1614
2 PLAC Rothesay
2 ADDR
3 CTRY Scotland
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''''Angus''''' married Mary, daughter of Hector Og Maclean of Duart, and had by her:
2 CONT 1. ''James''.
2 CONT 2.'' Angus Og.'' He married Katherine, daughter of Duncan Campbell of Danna, and had two sons, of whom nothing is known. He was in a most treacherous manner, with several of his followers, executed in the Grassmarket of Edinburgh,
2 CONC  8th July, 1615. 
2 CONT 3. ''Alexander Og'', who was drowned on Caol ile, Oct. 3, 1613. He left a natural daughter, Margaret, who
2 CONT married Hector M'Alister of Ardincross in 1626.
2 CONT 4. ''Mary'', who married Sir Donald Macdonald of Clanranald.
2 CONT 5. ''Margaret'', who married Ranald Macdouald of Benbecula.
2 CONT 6. ''Annabella'', who married Archibald Macdonald of Largie.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''''Angus Macdonald of Dunivaig''''' also had three natural sons:
2 CONT (a) '''''Archibald.'''''
2 CONT (b) ''Alexander.''
2 CONT (c) ''Ranald Og.''
2 CONT
2 CONT To''''' Archibald, known as Oilleasbuig Dubh''''', his father granted a charter in 1576 of the lands of Gigha for life. In 1582 he granted him a new charter of these lands and others, which in 1598 was confirmed by a charter from 
2 CONC the Crown. These lands, besides the 20 lands of Gigha, comprised 16 merklauds in Kintyre, 5 merklands in Islay, and 8 merklands in Knapdale, with the office of Toshachdorach of all the lands of Kintyre. Archibald was confined as a
2 CONC  hostage for his father and brother in the Castle of Dumbarton, from which he contrived to make his escapein 1607. Archibald Macdonald of Gigha died in 1618. According to MacVurich, "mhilleadh e an Eilein Mhic Carmaic agus chuirea
2 CONC dh a chorp ann an Cille Mhuire 'sa Chnap".
2 CONT He left three sons:
2 CONT (1) '''''John''''' who succeeded him.
2 CONT (2) ''Hugh'', who had two sons - Angus and James.
2 CONT (3) ''Archibald''.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''''Angus Macdonald of Dunnyveg''''' died at Rothesay, Oct. 21st, 1614, and was buried at Saddel.
2 CONT '''''Source: "The Clan Donald" Vol 3, page 378.'''''
2 CONT ----
