1 NOTE {geni:about_me} a.d.H. Peuth
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clodt_von__Jürgensburg
2 CONT
2 CONT The House Clodt von Jürgensburg (or Klodt; Russian: Клодт фон Юргенсбург) was a Russian noble family of Baltic German origin, whose members were prominent soldiers and artists.
2 CONT
2 CONT Notable members
2 CONT Baron Johan Adolf Clodt von Jürgensburg [sv], (1658–1720)
2 CONT Baron Gustaf Adolf Clodt von Jürgensburg (1692–1738), son of Johan Adolf
2 CONT Karl Gustav Clodt von Jürgensburg (1765–1822), colonel since 1806, participant in Patriotic War of 1812;
2 CONT Vladimir Clodt von Jürgensburg [sv] (1803–1887), professor of mathematics and general, chief of drawing department of the General Staff of Russian Army; son of Karl;
2 CONT Peter Clodt von Jürgensburg (1805–1867), prominent Russian sculptor, son of Karl;
2 CONT Konstantin Clodt von Jürgensburg [sv] (1807–1879), the first Russian wood engraver, son of Karl;
2 CONT Mikhail Petrovich Clodt von Jürgensburg [sv] (1835–1914), Russian painter, member of Peredvizhniki; son of Peter;
2 CONT Mikhail Konstantinovich Clodt von Jürgensburg (1832–1902); prominent realist painter; son of Konstantin;
2 CONT Elisabeth Järnefelt (née Clodt von Jürgensburg, 1839–1929); daughter of Konstantin; mother of Arvid, Eero and Armas Järnefelt, and Aino Sibelius;
2 CONT Nikolai Clodt von Jürgensburg (1865–1918) painter, grandson of Peter;
2 CONT Yevgeni Clodt von Jürgensburg [sv] (1867–1935), painter and jeweler, grandson of Konstantin;
2 CONT Pyotr Mikhailovich Clodt (1903–1942) painter, son of Mikhail Petrovich;
2 CONT References
2 CONT  "Клодт фон Юргенсбург, баронский род" . Brockhaus and Efron Encyclopedic Dictionary (in Russian). 1906.
2 CONT article Klodt von Jürgensburg (artists) on rulex encyclopedia (in Russian)
2 CONT All-Russia genealogical tree (in Russian)
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.familysearch.org/en/tree/person/details/GNC7-ST3
