1 NAME John /MacDonald of Clanranald/ Captain of Clanranald
2 GIVN John
2 SURN MacDonald of Clanranald
2 NSFX Captain of Clanranald
2 _MARNM MacDonald of Clanranald
1 SEX M
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1670
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == JOHN MACDONALD OF CLANRANALD ==
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Captain of Clanranald===
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT <blockquote>'''John Mackronnald of Moydort, Captain of Clanronnald (1625)  John Ranaldson Captain of Clanranald (1625) John McDonald McAllane Viceane, Captain of Clanronald (1627) John McRonald, son and heir of the late Sir Donald
2 CONC  McRonald of Ellantirme, knight (1628) John McDonald, Captain of Clanronald elder (1657)'''</blockquote>
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''John Macdonald of Clanranald, here treated, is the son of https://www.geni.com/people/Donald-MacDonald-10th-of-Clanranald/6000000013137996465?through=6000000013138117311. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/
2 CONC details.aspx?reference=GD201%2f1%2f17&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=&ko=p&r=GD201%2f1%2f17&ro=m&df=&dt=&di=n NRS: GD201/1/17]''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Evidence from the National Records of Scotland ==
2 CONT
2 CONT                     1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''28 April 1625: Instrument of Sasine in favour of Ronald McRonald of Castelvorff, uncle of John Mackronnald of Moydort, Captain of Clanronnald, in liferent and after his death heritably to Ronald McRonnald, his eldest son by Mar
2 CONC garet McDonald, daughter of the late Angus McDonald of Downnyvack, of the 13 penny lands of Borrow in Beanbecula and others, within the sheriffdom of Inverness as principal, and the 7 penny lands of Borrowneishivichtterach and oth
2 CONC ers in warrandice thereof in case of eviction; following upon a feu charter by John McDonald of Moydort dated 12 April 1625. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD201%2f1%2f10&st=1&tc=y&t
2 CONC l=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=&ko=p&r=GD201&ro=m&df=1620&dt=1670&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the MacDonald Family of Clanranald (Clanranald Papers), reference GD201/1/10]'''   
2 CONT
2 CONT                     2
2 CONT
2 CONT '''2 October 1625: Receipt by Alexander McEane Vic Eone Vic Donchie, servitor to the Lord of Lorne and to Mr Donald Campbell of Barbbrek Lochowe for 70 cows from John Ranaldson Captain of Clanranald, concerning a bargain. At Ellan
2 CONC e Tirrim. Witnesses: John Ranaldsone, parson of Ellanefynan; Allan Vic Cuk, apparent of Moroir; Donald Dwgailsone, vicar of Ellanefynan. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD201%2f1%2f13
2 CONC &st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=clanranald&ko=p&r=&ro=m&df=1620&dt=1670&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the MacDonald Family of Clanranald (Clanranald Papers), reference GD201/1/13]'''   
2 CONT
2 CONT                     3
2 CONT
2 CONT '''18 September 1627: Attested Copy Retour made in the Tolbooth of Inverness, finding John McDonald McAllane Viceane, Captain of Clanronald, heir to his father Sir Donald McAllane Viceane of Ellantirrim, in 21 merk lands in the Is
2 CONC land of Eggh, formerly granted to the late John McAlester, grandfather of the late Sir Donald, also to 3 merk lands of Moydort and others, all lying within the sheriffdom of Inverness united in the tenandry of Castletirrim, and th
2 CONC e above lands have been in the hands of the Crown by reason of non-entry since the death of Sir Donald in December 1619. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD201%2f1%2f17&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&
2 CONC tn=n&tp=n&k=&ko=p&r=GD201%2f1%2f17&ro=m&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the MacDonald Family of Clanranald, reference GD201/1/17]''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT                     4
2 CONT
2 CONT '''17 November 1628: Bond by Colin Earl of Seafort to Andrew Fraser, sheriff clerk of Invernes, for £1000 Scots, on condition that if he present to Andrew a precept from Chancery upon retour for infefting John McRonald, son and he
2 CONC ir of the late Sir Donald McRonald of Ellantirme, knight, in the lands of Moydart and others, and pay to the said Andrew the ward and other duties or sufficient for the relief of the sheriff of Inverness in the next Exchequer, the
2 CONC n the former part of the bond shall be null. At Chanonry of Ross. Discharge of the above bond, dated as above, 13 May 1630. [http://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD201%2f1%2f19&st=1&tc=y&tl=
2 CONC n&tn=n&tp=n&k=&ko=p&r=GD201&ro=m&df=&dt=&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the MacDonald Family of Clanranald, reference GD201/1/19]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT                     5
2 CONT
2 CONT '''12 October 1657: Extract registered discharge by Archibald, Marquis of Argyll, in favour of Donald McDonald, Captain of Clanronald younger, for himself and John McDonald, Captain of Clanronald elder, his father, of 17,000 merks
2 CONC  Scots in part payment of 20,000 merks Scots in bond between them dated 22 August 1657. [https://catalogue.nrscotland.gov.uk/nrsonlinecatalogue/details.aspx?reference=GD201%2f5%2f914&st=1&tc=y&tl=n&tn=n&tp=n&k=&ko=p&r=GD201&ro=m&d
2 CONC f=1620&dt=1670&di=n National Records of Scotland, Papers of the MacDonald Family of Clanranald, reference GD201/5/914]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
