1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''''John Macdonald II. of Gigha''''' was served heir to his father in March, 1619, in all his lands, as well as in the office of Toshachdorach. In 1629 he sold his lands of Knockrinsale in Isla to John Campbell, F
2 CONC iar of Calder, and in 1631 he disposed of almost all his property to Archibald, Lord Lorn. 
2 CONT He married Elizabeth, daughter of Sir William Stewart, Constable of Dumbarton Castle, and had by her:
2 CONT (a) ''Alexander,'' who held lands in Kintyre.
2 CONT (b)'' Archibald'', who also held lands in Kintyre.
2 CONT (c)''' ''Margaret''''', who married Colonel James Montgomery of Coilsfield, son of the 6th Earl of Eglinton.
2 CONT '''''Source: "The Clan Donald" Vol 3, page 379.'''''
2 CONT ----
